{%- endif %}
{%- if dashboard %}

To use the dashboard as well:

```bash
pip install "{{ package_name }}[app]"
```
{%- endif %}
{%- else -%}
```bash
pip install git+https://github.com/{{ github_org }}/{{ package_name }}
```
{%- endif %}

The default branch, `main`, is always the most recent release, so the command
above installs released code. To install in-progress work, ask for `devel`
explicitly:

```bash
pip install "git+https://github.com/{{ github_org }}/{{ package_name }}@devel"
```

